course: dictionary
lesson: 1084
title: Boyish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Boyish means like a boy, or young-looking and full of fun. Look at the clues around it: «He has a boyish face.» The man in this sentence looks young, so boyish is describing how he looks.
explain: «A boyish grin» is a cheeky, happy smile, the kind a boy might give after a joke. Swap in a word like playful to check: a playful grin still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Boyish does not always mean about boys. «A boyish haircut» is short and simple, like a boy's haircut, and a girl can have one. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad's boyish excitement about new crazes shows he is eager and foolish, like a child.
fact: Boyish means like a boy, or young-looking and full of fun.
fact: «A boyish grin» is a cheeky, happy smile.
fact: «He has a boyish face» can describe a grown man who looks young.
fact: «A boyish haircut» is a short, simple style, and anyone can have one.
fact: «Silly boyish amusement» means playful fun that is a bit foolish.
exercise: In «a boyish grin», what does boyish mean? | *Cheeky and happy, like a boy | Quiet and still | Very tall | Angry and cross
exercise: Toad's boyish excitement about new crazes makes him fun and foolish. What does boyish suggest about Toad? | Old and wise | *Eager and playful, like a child | Sleepy and tired
exercise: Can a girl have a boyish haircut? | No, haircuts cannot be boyish | Yes, but only if she is a boy | *Yes, because boyish can mean short and simple, like a boy's style | No, boyish only ever describes boys
test: In «He has a boyish face», what does boyish tell us? | He is very old | Ill and pale | He is wearing a hat | *He looks young and full of fun
test: Which word is closest in meaning to boyish in «silly boyish amusement»? | Tired | Gloomy | Serious | *Playful
exam: Read «a boyish grin» and choose the best meaning. | *Cheeky and happy | Cold and angry | Very large | Sad and gloomy
